<!-- wp:group {"align":"wide","className":"longevity-section","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} --><div class="wp-block-group alignwide longevity-section"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"longevity-kicker"} --><p class="longevity-kicker">How Consumer Lab works</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">A decision record, not a decorative score</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"longevity-section-intro"} --><p class="longevity-section-intro">A written protocol does not mean a product has been tested. Tested presentation appears only after the completed record is approved and version-matched.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><div class="longevity-testing-steps"><article class="longevity-testing-step"><h3>Define the protocol</h3><p>Set the observations, comparisons, conditions, and scoring model before testing.</p></article><article class="longevity-testing-step"><h3>Acquire and test</h3><p>Record the actual model, acquisition route, dates, environment, deviations, and failures.</p></article><article class="longevity-testing-step"><h3>Review the record</h3><p>Check the evidence, score, limitations, disclosure, and any required medical-review scope.</p></article><article class="longevity-testing-step"><h3>Publish the decision</h3><p>Expose the approved bounded results, confidence, method, and correction path.</p></article></div><!-- /wp:html --></div><!-- /wp:group -->
